<Document>
<name>C45TA51 Ver001 luminous trajectory - MEDIAN (weighted mean) arrival</name>
<description>C45TA51 Ver001: projected luminous trajectory for the MEDIAN (weighted mean) arrival. Straight line from 90 km to 20 km above the ground, between the points where the estimated gravity-curved path (through the 110 km point 32.011 N, -110.618 E at 2026-02-08 08:34:56.8 UTC) reaches those heights. Speeds are relative to the rotating Earth: 35.50 km/s down to 95 km, then constant deceleration 8.14 km/s^2 (831 g) to 3.0 km/s at 20 km. Luminous path length 71.7 km, duration 3.8 s. Estimated, not observed: the direction comes from the Meerkat e-mail analysis, there is no ablation/fragmentation model, ground taken at the WGS84 ellipsoid. The e-mail is confidential and the object unconfirmed: do not distribute.</description>
